shoot:description:This gallery covers most of September, which is a great birding month with many birds still around and some good ones passing through.  
shoot:favorite:2026-09-11-094438-74-R5PT5902-sm.jpg
2026-09-17-093145-67-R5PT6607-sm.jpg:desciption:I didn't get to see if this bird was able to swallow the frog.  I havne't seen one going after prey that large!  I bet it was able to get it down, but it ran out of sight.
2026-09-18-104232-66-R5PT6682-sm.jpg:description:This was a cool looking turkey!  Lots of leucism, but still plenty of dark color on the feathers as well.
2026-09-24-161310-32-R5PT7040-sm.jpg:description:This Jay has been hanging around for a while now.  It's got a bit of white above both eyes, so I'm hoping to get some better photos.  It might be a cross with a southwestern Steller's Jay, or it might just have some minor leucism.
2026-09-24-161344-97-R5PT7086-sm.jpg:description:New yard bird!  This flock flew over the neighborhood.
